    "narrative": "Our primary objective today is capitalizing on the favorable matchup against Bradford, which elevates **Zack Gelof** (66.86) and **Lawrence Butler** (60.01) into our high-priority start tier. **Zack Gelof** is our premier play, benefiting from a massive 19% SP skill boost and a 7% platoon advantage that outweighs the modest base projection. While **Lawrence Butler** faces a slight regression for the L/L matchup, the sheer weakness of the opposing arm keeps him well within our \"Strong\" start threshold. Conversely, the high-upside play of the day is **Dylan Beavers** (68.38); despite hitting lower in the order, he is thriving in an excellent park environment against a favorable arm, making him a must-start as we hunt for his elite sprint speed and counting stats. **Bryce Harper** (66.94) remains the anchor of our lineup, with his premium spot in the order and a favorable 4.09 xERA matchup solidifying him as a cornerstone.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was leaving **Jonathan Aranda** (47.17) out of the starting nine. While his platoon edge against Hagenman offered potential, his limited park factors and the superior projected efficiency of our current outfield mix pushed him just outside the active roster. We are closely monitoring the status of **Will Smith** and **Alex Freeland**, as their scores are currently based on pending lineups; should **Will Smith** drop lower in the order, his utility score could dip significantly. We also note a major caution with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (48.68); while he is a lineup lock, he is facing the stiffest test of the day against Cease (2.97 xERA). His BvP struggles and the elite opponent skill have dragged his efficiency down, so we will need him to outperform his projection to sustain our offensive momentum. Finally, we remain clear of **Tyler Freeman** and **Cal Raleigh** today, as both remain unavailable due to minor league assignments or rest, ensuring our active slots are optimized for pure daily production.",
